{
  "suite": "money.allocate",
  "spec": "0.1.0",
  "description": "Split an amount so parts sum exactly to the input, by largest remainder with ties to the lower index (spec 3.7). A negative amount allocates its magnitude and negates each part. An empty ratio list and an all-zero ratio list are rejected with HEPH-MONEY-422; negative ratios are not representable.",
  "source": "Hand-derived arithmetic; exact large values checked by integer division only. 100/[3,1,2]: shares 50, 16.667, 33.333, floors 50,16,33 sum 99, one leftover unit to index 1 (remainder 2/3 is largest) giving 50,17,33 (sequential would give 51,16,33). 1000/[1 x7]: 142.857 each, floors 142 x7 = 994, six leftover units, all remainders tie so indices 0-5 get one each: 143 x6 + 142 = 1000. 9223372036854775807/[2,1]: amount*2 = 18446744073709551614 overflows i64; floors 6148914691236517204 and 3074457345618258602 sum to 9223372036854775806; remainders 2/3 and 1/3, so the one leftover unit goes to index 0 giving 6148914691236517205 + 3074457345618258602 = 9223372036854775807. Ratios stay within 0..2^53-1 so they survive JavaScript numbers.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "kes-100-by-1-1-1",
      "input": {
        "money": {
          "amount": "100",
          "currency": "KES"
        },
        "ratios": [
          1,
          1,
          1
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "amount": "34",
            "currency": "KES"
          },
          {
            "amount": "33",
            "currency": "KES"
          },
          {
            "amount": "33",
            "currency": "KES"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
